---
/**
 * /en/privacy-policy/ — versão em inglês de /politica-de-privacidade/.
 * Manter sincronizada com src/pages/politica-de-privacidade.astro: qualquer
 * mudança de conteúdo lá precisa ser feita aqui também.
 */
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '~/lib/site';
import '~/styles/politica.css';

const secoes = [
  { id: 'quem-trata', rotulo: 'Who processes your data' },
  { id: 'dados', rotulo: 'What data we collect' },
  { id: 'finalidade', rotulo: 'What we use it for' },
  { id: 'base-legal', rotulo: 'On what legal basis' },
  { id: 'sigilo', rotulo: 'Attorney confidentiality' },
  { id: 'compartilhamento', rotulo: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'prazo', rotulo: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'direitos', rotulo: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'encarregado', rotulo: 'Data protection officer' },
  { id: 'seguranca', rotulo: 'Security' },
  { id: 'mudancas', rotulo: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'falar', rotulo: 'How to reach us' },
];
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  alternativa="/politica-de-privacidade/"
  sobreposto={false}
  titulo="Privacy Policy | Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados"
  descricao="How Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados handles the personal data of people who use this website: what data is collected, for what purpose, on what legal basis, and what your rights are."
>
  <article class="politica">
    <div class="env">
      <p class="chapeu">Legal document</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="atualizado" data-placeholder="1">
        <span class="marca-falta">To be defined</span>
        Date of last update to be filled in when the firm approves the final text.
      </p>

      <div class="ressalva">
        <p>
          <strong>This text is still provisional.</strong> It follows the structure
          required by the LGPD (Brazil's General Data Protection Law, Law
          13,709/2018) and describes what this website actually does. The passages
          in red depend on a decision by the firm and are marked as such. The final
          text will come from the partners.
        </p>
      </div>

      <nav class="sumario" aria-label="Sections of this policy">
        <h2>On this page</h2>
        <ol>
          {secoes.map((secao) => (
            <li><a href={`#${secao.id}`}>{secao.rotulo}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="texto">
        <p>
          This policy explains what happens to your data when you use this website,
          especially when you fill out the contact form or sign up for our article
          mailing list. It describes how the website really works and was written to
          be read.
        </p>

        <h2 id="quem-trata">Who processes your data</h2>
        <p>
          The data controller, as defined in Article 5, VI, of Law 13,709/2018, is the
          law firm below. The controller is the party that decides what is collected
          and for what purpose.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>{site.nomeSociedade}</li>
          <li data-placeholder={site.registro.oabSociedade.placeholder ? '1' : undefined}>
            Registration with the OAB (the Brazilian Bar Association): {site.registro.oabSociedade.valor}
          </li>
          <li data-placeholder={site.registro.cnpj.placeholder ? '1' : undefined}>
            CNPJ (Brazilian company registration number) {site.registro.cnpj.valor}
          </li>
          <li data-placeholder={site.email.placeholder ? '1' : undefined}>
            Email: {site.email.valor}
          </li>
          <li>{site.cidade}, {site.estado}</li>
        </ul>
        <p data-placeholder="1">
          <span class="marca-falta">To be defined</span>
          Full address of the main office to be filled in. The firm has not yet
          provided the address for in-person meetings.
        </p>

        <h2 id="dados">What data we collect</h2>
        <h3>Data you give us</h3>
        <p>
          These are the fields of the contact form, and only those. No other data is
          requested anywhere else on the website:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Name:</strong> so we know how to address you in our reply.</li>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> so we can reply.</li>
          <li><strong>Phone:</strong> optional, if you prefer to be contacted by phone.</li>
          <li><strong>Subject:</strong> optional, to give context before we read your message.</li>
          <li><strong>Message:</strong> whatever you write.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you sign up for our article mailing list, we collect <strong>only your
          email address</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you prefer to talk over WhatsApp, the conversation takes place inside the
          app and is governed by the platform's privacy policy, over which we have no
          control. Whatever you write to us there is handled by us with the same care
          described here.
        </p>

        <h3>Data collected automatically</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>At this time, none.</strong> No analytics tool is enabled on this
          website: no Google Analytics, no heat map, no social media pixel. The cookie
          notice asks for your choice and stores your answer in your own browser, so it
          doesn't ask again on every page, and that answer never leaves your device.
        </p>
        <p data-placeholder="1">
          <span class="marca-falta">To be defined</span>
          Whether the firm will measure visits to the website and, if so, with which
          tool. Until that decision is made, this policy names no measurement tool,
          because none is in use. On the day one is enabled, this passage and the{' '}
          <a href="/en/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a> must be updated first.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not ask for sensitive data</strong> in the form, as defined in
          Article 5, II, of the LGPD. A message you send us may still contain sensitive
          information by the very nature of the matter, and in that case it is handled
          under the attorney confidentiality described below.
        </p>

        <h2 id="finalidade">What we use it for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Reading your message and replying.</li>
          <li>Continuing the conversation about the matter you brought to us.</li>
          <li>Sending the articles on our mailing list, if you asked for them.</li>
          <li>Keeping the website running and protected against automated submissions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not sell your data</strong>, we do not hand it over for
          third-party advertising, and we do not use your email address for messages
          you did not ask for.
        </p>

        <h2 id="base-legal">On what legal basis</h2>
        <p>The LGPD requires a justification for each processing activity. Ours are:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Preliminary procedures related to a contract</strong>
            (Article 7, V): when you write to us asking for guidance, processing your
            data is what allows us to reply.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent</strong> (Article 7, I): for the article mailing list, which
            is sent only to those who asked for it, and for any cookie that is not
            necessary for the website to work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Compliance with a legal or regulatory obligation</strong> (Article
            7, II): for what the law and the rules of the OAB require us to record and
            keep.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Regular exercise of rights</strong> (Article 7, VI): to keep a
            record of what was discussed, should it become necessary in legal
            proceedings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate interest</strong> (Article 7, IX): to protect the website
            against abuse, such as automated form submissions by bots.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="sigilo">Attorney confidentiality</h2>
        <p>
          What you tell us is protected by attorney confidentiality, a duty set out in
          Article 34, VII, of the Brazilian Attorneys' Statute (Estatuto da Advocacia,
          Law 8,906/1994) and in the OAB Code of Ethics and Discipline. This duty is
          stricter than the LGPD and does not depend on your having hired the firm: it
          applies from the very first message.
        </p>
        <p>
          In practice, this means that the content of what you write is not discussed
          outside the firm, is not used as an example, and does not appear in any of
          our publications.
        </p>

        <h2 id="compartilhamento">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          Only with those needed for the website to work. They are technology
          providers, who process the data on our behalf and may not use it for their
          own purposes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Vercel:</strong> hosts the website and delivers it to your browser.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Brevo:</strong> sends the firm the message you wrote in the form,
            sends you the confirmation of receipt, and manages the article mailing list.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          No advertising service receives data from this website, under any
          circumstances.
        </p>
        <p>
          The two providers above keep servers outside Brazil, which constitutes an{' '}
          <strong>international transfer of data</strong> (Article 33 of the LGPD).
        </p>
        <p>
          Other than that, we share data only when required by law or a court order,
          and within the limits allowed by attorney confidentiality.
        </p>

        <h2 id="prazo">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p data-placeholder="1">
          <span class="marca-falta">To be defined</span>
          The retention periods for each type of data are to be defined by the firm.
          This decision combines statutes of limitations, the attorney's duty to keep
          records, and the firm's internal policy, and it is not for whoever built the
          website to settle. Until the periods are defined, this policy states no
          figure.
        </p>
        <p>
          What already applies, regardless of the period chosen: the email address on
          the article mailing list is kept until you unsubscribe, and the link to do so
          is in the footer of every message. Once the period for each piece of data has
          passed, it is deleted or anonymized.
        </p>

        <h2 id="direitos">Your rights</h2>
        <p>Article 18 of the LGPD ensures that you may, at any time, ask us to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>confirm</strong> whether we process your data and give you <strong>access</strong> to it;</li>
          <li><strong>correct</strong> incomplete, inaccurate, or outdated data;</li>
          <li><strong>anonymize, block, or delete</strong> data that is unnecessary or processed in breach of the law;</li>
          <li><strong>port</strong> your data to another provider;</li>
          <li><strong>delete</strong> data processed on the basis of your consent;</li>
          <li><strong>tell you who</strong> we share your data with;</li>
          <li><strong>withdraw your consent</strong>, without invalidating the processing carried out before;</li>
          <li><strong>object</strong> to processing you consider improper.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some of these requests are limited by the attorney's duty to keep records and
          by attorney confidentiality. When that is the case, we explain what the limit
          is and why it exists, instead of simply refusing.
        </p>
        <p data-placeholder="1">
          <span class="marca-falta">To be defined</span>
          Response time for data subject requests to be defined by the firm. The LGPD
          sets a deadline only for requests for confirmation and access in simplified
          form (fifteen days, Article 19, I). For the others, the deadline is whatever
          the firm commits to, and it has not committed to one yet.
        </p>

        <h2 id="encarregado">Data protection officer</h2>
        <p>
          Article 41 of the LGPD requires the controller to appoint the person to
          contact about data protection, and to make that appointment public.
        </p>
        <p data-placeholder="1">
          <span class="marca-falta">To be defined</span>
          Who the firm's data protection officer (encarregado) is and through which
          channel they can be reached. The appointment is the partners' decision. Until
          it is made, this policy names no one, because naming the wrong person is
          worse than admitting that the appointment is pending.
        </p>

        <h2 id="seguranca">Security</h2>
        <p>
          The website is served entirely over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). The form
          is protected against automated submissions and limits the number of
          submissions per device. Access to the messages received is restricted to
          people who work at the firm.
        </p>
        <p>
          No system is immune to incidents. If one occurs that may pose a significant
          risk to you, we will notify you and the ANPD (the Brazilian data protection
          authority), as required by Article 48 of the LGPD.
        </p>

        <h2 id="mudancas">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If the website starts doing something different with your data, this text
          changes accordingly, and so does the date at the top of the page. Significant
          changes are announced on the website itself.
        </p>

        <h2 id="falar">How to reach us</h2>
        <p>
          For any questions about privacy, or to exercise the rights above, write to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email.valor}`} data-placeholder={site.email.placeholder ? '1' : undefined}>{site.email.valor}</a>{' '}
          or use the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may also file a complaint directly with the{' '}
          <a href="https://www.gov.br/anpd/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ANPD</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
